  "description": "Use the ordinary generic Peptone identity mesh:D010461 (Peptones) under MAPPING_SEMANTICS section3 exact-term and unspecified-sense priority. The active primary NLM descriptor explicitly supplies Peptone as an entry term and a conventional water-soluble partial protein-hydrolysis material definition, independently consistent with the manufacturer generic peptone description. The earlier requirement for a source-specific acid-or-enzyme/precipitation certificate was overstated: the general possibility of base hydrolysis does not establish a different actual preparation or sense for this unqualified owner. This is generic material identity, not identity with every supplier product or a newly verified assay preparation. The earlier FoodOn inference was also overstated: its actual member_of external category relation is not a has-role, food-use, regulatory-approval or lot-eligibility requirement, and the axiom alone does not refute a material broader mapping. The closer direct generic MeSH term, rather than that invented gate, determines the corrected identity choice. Retain all earlier evidence and histories as authentic superseded interpretation; preserve raw plural and rejected truncated label, occurrence statistics, provisional roles and all frozen source/owner/export holds. Five reviewed generic dependent references and the separate RCM reference must follow this actual identifier in independently authored source-specific successors; no global replacement, named-product merge or source-observation redirect is authorized.",
