  "direct_term_predecessor_description": "Reconcile existing generic Peptone owner to local protein-digest material identity, removing unsupported exact mammalian MICRO0000178 scope. Keep raw plural provenance, all existing role/count/truncated-alias holds and both MicrobeDecoder source-case holds; no new owner or catalog assignment. Final correction: Correct the exact campaign MappingEvidence method under issue 1226 to LLM_SUGGESTION; preserve its source and claim. Inherited human/process evidence and ComponentEvidence types are unchanged. Reject only the incomplete concentration token Peptone (0.01 % as an identity name of generic Peptone. Preserve its original microbedecoder provenance and plural Peptones. Do not invent a missing parenthesis, percent basis or preparation. Eighteen retained historical inbound MICRO:0000178 component references and current proposed components remain a source-level integration dependency; no automatic retargeting is authorized. Consolidated parent-grounding successor: Complete the supported nonidentity family grounding: retain kgmicrobe.ingredient:peptone and use NARROW_MATCH to mesh:D011492 Protein Hydrolysates, with native broadMatch plus the local B1 identity row. The active primary NLM concept M0017860 defines a complex mixture produced by partial or extensive hydrolysis; the manufacturer guide defines generic peptones as water-soluble partial protein hydrolysates and includes plant, yeast or animal material and acid, base or enzyme processing. Assess the direct MeSH Peptones term D010461 before this broader route: its acid-or-enzyme and precipitation criteria are not established for the complete source-unspecified generic scope. MICRO:0000178 adds unsupported mammalian origin, MICRO:0000174 an unverified enzymatic process, and MICRO:0000172 does not establish yeast coverage. Do not select FOODON:03315306 after full OWL inspection reveals an actual member-of food-additive restriction in addition to its SIREN comment; preserve the initial private candidate and NEW01 report as unselected evidence. CHEBI:749541 is a sparse imported molecular-entity class without established whole-mixture scope. MICRO:0000167 is a supported but less specific undefined-mixture option. The MeSH descriptor indexing annotation about therapeutic/nutrient use is not imported as a clinical or assay role. Preserve the two MicrobeDecoder observations, raw plural, rejected truncated token, all previous history/evidence/statistics, provisional roles, source holds and source-specific incoming-reference reconciliation; no owner, source-case or export admission.",
  "direct_term_successor_author": "/root/buffer_hepes",
